Found by the worker in k130, confirmed in its review. On Linux the editor-path check in cmd/launcher/helpers.go (pathFound, fileExists = os.Stat) accepts an existing file without the execute bit, or a directory, as unreal.editor, although exec.Command then fails with permission denied. k130 deliberately kept os.Stat off Windows so Linux behaviour stayed byte-for-byte. Dev-box only (the product target is Windows), so low value. Fix sketch: off Windows, also warn when the path is a directory or has no execute bit, with a message that says so rather than "path not found". Done when the warning matches what exec.Command does on Linux, pinned by a test.

**Decision 2026-11-21 (main agent):** off Windows, a directory or a file with no execute bit named as unreal.editor gets its own warning naming the cause ("is a directory", "is not executable"), not "not found". It stays a warning, the same severity as today's. Windows is unchanged. k178 follows it, also in helpers.go.

